  "name": "Then (Tày, Nùng and Thái ritual song)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Ritual practice of the Tày, Nùng and Thái peoples of northern Vietnam, inscribed by UNESCO in 2019, in which a then master sings long song cycles narrating a journey to the heavenly realm to pray for peace, healing and good harvests. The master accompanies the singing on the đàn tính, a long-necked lute with a gourd body, and shakes a cluster of small bells (chùm xóc nhạc). The đàn tam card stands in for the đàn tính and the shaker card for the bell cluster.",
  "recipe": "classic late-2010s then, ritual Devotional, indigenous branch. solo with instrumental accompaniment, single lead single track no stacking. dan tam, shaker source unspecified. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
